\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1.We rose to- day with anthems sweet
\par To sing before the mercy- seat,
\par And ere the darkness round us fell
\par We bade the grateful vespers swell.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Whate'er has risen from heart 
\par sincere,
\par Each upward glance of filial fear,
\par Each true resolve, each solemn vow,
\par Jesus our Lord, accept it now.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Whate'er beneath Thy searching 
\par eyes,
\par Has wrought to spoil our sacrifice,
\par Mid this sweet stillness while we bow,
\par Jesus our Lord, forgive us now,
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4.O teach us erring souls to win,
\par And hide a multitude of sin,
\par To tread in Christ's long- suffering
\par way,
\par And grow more like Him day by day.
\par                                      Amen.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

